endure:
Of hens, the wheeze of a pump, she needs must hear;
She inescapably must endure to feel
Across her teeth the grinding of a backing wagon

enduring:
Her likeness! Would that I might limn it,
As Love did, with enduring art;
Nor dust of days nor death may dim it,

I too might feel that frenzied faith whose touch
Makes temporal the most enduring grief;
Though it must walk a while, as is its wont,

ender:
I am the mother of sorrows,
I am the ender of grief;
I am the bud and the blossom,

endear:
The reefs in old Gethsemane
Endear the shore beyond.
'T is beggars banquets best define;

endears:
Far ends of tired days;
It half endears the abstinence,
And pain is missed in praise.
